{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793396459,"nonce":"8h//gjxKZCj10KlGoNMgP1IUEnw=","title":"cn visual fidelity: reach ashui's component stylesheet, starting with the CSS Blinc cannot parse yet","message":"ashui's component stylesheet (ashui/components/css/components.css, 1,449 lines, plus ashui/haxe/ashui/css/UserAgent.hx, 348) is the visual spec for cn. It has been cleaned of many styling bugs that blinc_cn still has. Component defaults, variants and states are all rules in that sheet: --ui-\u003ccomponent\u003e-* override variables with theme fallbacks, [data-variant] and [data-size] attribute selectors, :hover/:active/:focus-visible, color-mix() tints. cn_styles.rs (CN_STYLES, now an @layer) is the equivalent, but most of cn's state and variant looks still come from Rust (Stateful FSM, ButtonConfig).\n\nProbe, Blinc's parser over ashui's components.css with the default theme's variables seeded: 566 rules parse, 151 diagnostics. Grouped by cause, most important first:\n\n- color-mix(in srgb, \u003ccolor\u003e N%, \u003ccolor|transparent\u003e): about 35 rules. These are the hover and active tints on outline, ghost, secondary and destructive variants, so no fidelity without it.\n- box-shadow with a var() that resolves empty (22): the theme's CSS variable map lacks the shadow tokens ashui reads (--shadow-sm/md/lg), or they are not serialised as a box-shadow value.\n- transform: none (27) and an empty transform (4): reset values are rejected, which blocks :active scale(0.97) and its reset on link buttons.\n- Per-side borders: border-top/right/bottom/left and their -width/-color longhands (about 20). Needed by tables, tabs, sidebar, accordion.\n- currentColor (3), font-size: inherit, letter-spacing in em (-0.025em, 0.04em, 0.05em).\n- Layout values: display: grid and grid-template-columns/grid-column/grid-row (3 rules), margin: auto, max-width: none|100%, min-height: 100%, flex-basis, row-gap/column-gap, three-value padding and margin shorthands.\n- Custom properties declared inside a rule (--ui-button-height etc.), not only in :root. ashui overrides components through these.\n- linear-gradient with percentage stops containing negative or \u003e100% positions (skeleton shimmer).\n- font-family in a rule.\n\nNot yet checked, probably also gaps: whether [data-variant=\"x\"] attribute selectors match, :focus-visible, and a transition on state changes.\n\nPlan, each step lands alone with a render test:\n1. Parser/value gaps above, in the order listed. A snapshot test per construct.\n2. Seed theme variables ashui reads (shadow tokens, --text-inverse, --primary-hover/active, --secondary-*, --error) so var() resolves. Diff the variable names ashui reads against ThemeState::to_css_variable_map.\n3. Port component rules into cn_styles.rs one component at a time (Button first), check against ashui's snapshot of the same scene (ashui tools/snapshot/run.sh renders a scene to PNG; ash is built at ../ash) using blinc's offscreen capture.\n4. Move state colours from Rust (ButtonConfig hover/pressed/disabled) to :hover/:active/:disabled rules; Button stops binding its own bg. This is the first slice of 2c565dc.\n5. Delete the Rust defaults that the sheet now owns, once the sheet is mandatory for cn.\n\nRelated: 7cabafe, 6f7b001, 2c565dc, 7d2d6eb.","files":null}]}